From 1a652983ea16f636aa27139c3ea32f12f9ccd5fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:05:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] core-update pause: cancel a long model request at a
 step boundary (t_01a1d293248f5e12)

hermes-hub 2026-11-13 01:22:19-01:25:08: a Desktop turn sat in a 169 s model request
right after its tool results. The update pause lands only at a step boundary and the
mid-tool cancel covered tool calls and compressions, so the turn kept its admission
reservation unpublished and every instant apply after the 60 s cap was refused
('1 unpublished reservation(s)'); the update applied 274 s after it was due.

A model request issued at a step boundary (an earlier call ran this turn and the
transcript ends on a tool result) now registers with agent.update_pause_cancel as
'model-request'. After MID_TOOL_GRACE_S the watcher cancels it; the request's output
(partial, crossed response, or a provider error caused by the cancel) is dropped and
the same logical iteration is re-issued through the redirect restart, so
begin_iteration takes the pending cancel and pauses at that boundary (resumable,
reservation released). The turn's first request is not a boundary and is untouched;
a user Stop still wins.
